    "body": "### Problem\n\nFollow-up to #42205, after #42312. NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1952+g187d13aa60.\n\n\nThe `nvim_put()` repro in #42205 is fixed.\n\nHowever, I'm using mini.snippets which ends each expansion with `call complete(col(\".\"), [])` to hide the popup. Completion is then active with no candidates. The API edit is dropped at `<Esc>`.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\n-- nvim --clean -u minimal.lua\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-j>', function()\n  vim.api.nvim_put({ 'X' }, 'c', false, true)\n  vim.cmd('silent noautocmd call complete(col(\".\"), [])')\nend)\n```\n\nBuffer:\n\n```\nfoo\nbar\n```\n\nType `QjQA<C-j><Esc>`.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nAfter `<C-j>`: `fooX` / `barX`. After `<Esc>`:\n\n```\nfoo\nbarX\n```\n\nAlso:\n\n- `complete()` before or after `nvim_put()`: same result.\n- Typed text after the mapping is kept. `QjQA<C-j>Y<Esc>` gives `fooY` / `barXY`.\n- `complete(col(\".\"), [])` alone is harmless.\n- A real completion works. `complete(col(\".\"), ['X'])` then `<Esc>` gives `fooX` / `barX`.\n- A real completion plus an API edit fails. `nvim_put({'X'})` then `complete(col(\".\"), ['Y'])`, then `<C-y><Esc>` gives `fooY` / `barXY`.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n\n```\nfooX\nbarX\n```\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1952+g187d13aa60\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacos\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from main branch",
